<article class="env-lemma" id="04FA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04FA">Lemma <span data-tag="04FA">37.7.8</span>.</a> Taking the universal first order thickenings commutes with taking opens. More precisely, let $h : Z \to X$ be a formally unramified morphism of schemes. Let $V \subset Z$, $U \subset X$ be opens such that $h(V) \subset U$. Let $Z'$ be the universal first order thickening of $Z$ over $X$. Then $h|_ V : V \to U$ is formally unramified and the universal first order thickening of $V$ over $U$ is the open subscheme $V' \subset Z'$ such that $V = Z \cap V'$. In particular, $\mathcal{C}_{Z/X}|_ V = \mathcal{C}_{V/U}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first statement is Lemma <a href="/tag/02HC" data-tag="02HC">37.6.5</a>. The compatibility of universal thickenings can be deduced from the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/04F3" data-tag="04F3">37.7.1</a>, or from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/04EE" data-tag="04EE">10.149.4</a> or deduced from Lemma <a href="/tag/04F9" data-tag="04F9">37.7.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>